{title: Speak, LORD}
{subtitle: 1 Samuel 3:1–10; 1:9–28; 16:1–13}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 74}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] [Bbsus4] | [Ab] |
| [Bbsus4] [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Hannah wept at Shiloh and her [Bb/D]lips moved with no sound
Old [Cm7]Eli thought she'd had the wine, but [Ab]grief had brought her down
She [Eb]came back with a little boy and [Bb/D]gave him with both hands
[Cm7]I prayed for this child
So now [Ab]I give him to the [Bb]LORD
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]In those days the word of the LORD [Bb/D]was rare
The [Cm7]lamp of God had not yet gone out [Ab]
The [Eb]boy lay in the temple in the qui[Bb/D]et midnight air
When a [Cm7]voice called out his name and he ran [Ab]to Eli's [Bb]side
Here I [Ab]am; you called [Bb]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Speak, LORD, for [Bb/D]your servant is listening
[Cm7]In the stillness of the [Ab]night [Eb]
Speak, LORD, [Bb/D]for your servant is listening
[Cm7]Till the lamp gives way [Ab]to light [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Years went by and Samuel came with oil [Bb/D]to Bethlehem
[Cm7]Seven sons passed by him, and the LORD [Ab]chose none of them
They [Eb]sent out for the youngest one who kept [Bb/D]the sheep that day
[Cm7]Rise and anoint him; this [Ab]is the [Bb]one
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]Man looks at the outward appear[Bb]ance
But [Eb]the LORD looks [Bb/D]at the [Cm7]heart
[Ab]Man looks at the outward appear[Bb]ance
But [Eb]the LORD looks [Bb/D]at the [Cm7]heart [Eb]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Speak, LORD, [Bb/D]for your servant is listening
[Cm7]In the stillness of the [Ab]night [Eb]
Speak, LORD, [Bb/D]for your servant is listening
[Cm7]Till the lamp gives way [Ab]to light
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]Speak, LORD [Bb/D]
For [Cm7]your servant is listening
{end_of_verse}
